# Analysis > Structure and Defects > Dislocation Post-Processing: a perfect
# Cu crystal and the same crystal with an edge dislocation (Edit > Insert
# Dislocation), compared by the Nye tensor, the Vitek map, pattern matching,
# drag preparation and the dislocation fit; results exported as CSV. The
# expected numbers are the command line's (atomforge --analyze nye, vitek,
# pattern-init/pattern-detect, drag, fit-dislocation) on the same files.
open docs/manual/examples/cu_fcc.cif
step replicate
set counts 6 6 6
apply
save rust/target/ui/disl_reference.cif
dislocation set character edge
dislocation generate
dislocation replace
save rust/target/ui/disl_deformed.cif
dialog dislocation-analysis open
dialog dislocation-analysis reference rust/target/ui/no_such_file.cif
dialog dislocation-analysis expect-error no_such_file
dialog dislocation-analysis reference rust/target/ui/disl_reference.cif
dialog dislocation-analysis deformed rust/target/ui/disl_deformed.cif
dialog dislocation-analysis nye 3.0
dialog dislocation-analysis expect-nye-max 3.1660609793459904
dialog dislocation-analysis expect-nye-top 21
dialog dislocation-analysis export nye rust/target/ui/disl_nye.csv
dialog dislocation-analysis vitek 0 0 1 2.55
dialog dislocation-analysis expect-vitek-pairs 10368 10368
dialog dislocation-analysis export vitek rust/target/ui/disl_vitek.csv
dialog dislocation-analysis pattern 3.2 10
dialog dislocation-analysis expect-unmatched 417 417
dialog dislocation-analysis export pattern rust/target/ui/disl_pattern.csv
dialog dislocation-analysis drag 0.5
dialog dislocation-analysis expect-drag-atoms 864
dialog dislocation-analysis export drag rust/target/ui/disl_drag.cif
dialog dislocation-analysis fit 0 0 1 3 1
dialog dislocation-analysis expect-fit-position 8.4944112498720408 8.8860766037922279 8.8726477108439603
dialog dislocation-analysis expect-fit-burgers 0 0.000001
wait 2
screenshot rust/target/ui/dislocation_analysis.png
quit
